('127.402.d.7.E',4,'If testing shows that users care more about comfort than weight, the team should:','["keep it unchanged", "blame users", "modify the statement to include comfort", "hide the data"]'::jsonb,2,'Update with learning.','original'),
('127.402.d.7.F',3,'A design brief is a document that outlines the:','["game rules", "seating chart", "lunch menu", "problem, goals, and constraints of a project"]'::jsonb,3,'Briefs define the project.','original'),
('127.402.d.7.F',4,'A design brief helps a team stay on track by describing the:','["requirements the solution must meet", "team members'' hobbies", "company logo", "weather"]'::jsonb,0,'Requirements guide design.','original'),
('127.402.d.7.G',3,'A technical document should include a problem statement, constraints, and:','["slogans", "criteria for success", "jokes", "menus"]'::jsonb,1,'Criteria define success.','original'),
('127.402.d.7.G',4,'A well-compiled design brief is written so that a new team member can:','["guess the goal", "need a translator", "understand the project without extra explanation", "do nothing"]'::jsonb,2,'Clear documents stand alone.','original'),
('127.402.d.8.A',3,'Creativity in engineering helps teams to:','["repeat errors", "copy exactly", "avoid thinking", "find new solutions to problems"]'::jsonb,3,'Creativity drives innovation.','original'),
('127.402.d.8.A',4,'Innovation differs from invention because innovation:','["puts a new idea to practical, valuable use", "requires a patent", "is always a physical device", "is always small"]'::jsonb,0,'Innovation applies ideas.','original'),
('127.402.d.8.B',3,'In brainstorming, a rule is to:','["pick one idea only", "withhold judgment while ideas are generated", "criticize every idea", "stay silent"]'::jsonb,1,'Defer judgment.','original'),
('127.402.d.8.B',4,'SCAMPER is a technique that prompts new ideas by asking how to substitute, combine, adapt, modify, put to other uses, eliminate, or:','["cancel", "delete files", "reverse", "repeat"]'::jsonb,2,'R is rearrange or reverse.','original'),
('127.402.d.8.C',3,'Designing a product for a client differs from designing for oneself because the designer must meet the:','["random tastes", "calendar", "designer''s whims only", "client''s needs"]'::jsonb,3,'Clients define requirements.','original'),
('127.402.d.8.C',4,'When a client''s wishes conflict with safety, the engineer should:','["explain the risk and propose a safe alternative", "do as told", "quit silently", "ignore safety"]'::jsonb,0,'Safety remains non-negotiable.','original'),
('127.402.d.8.D',3,'A solution can be evaluated with criteria such as strength, cost, and:','["the team''s color", "ease of manufacture", "the song", "the date"]'::jsonb,1,'Evaluate with relevant criteria.','original'),
('127.402.d.8.D',4,'Comparing two bracket designs by testing which holds the heavier load is an evaluation of:','["appearance", "weight of the box", "structural strength", "name"]'::jsonb,2,'Load tests measure strength.','original'),
