('127.403.d.8.E',3,'Converting a hand-operated press to automatic requires adding sensors, actuators, and:','["a longer handle", "fewer parts", "more paint", "a controller with code"]'::jsonb,3,'Automation needs control.','original'),
('127.403.d.8.E',4,'A limit switch on an automated press tells the controller that the part is:','["in position", "late", "wet", "too heavy"]'::jsonb,0,'Switches give position feedback.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.A',3,'Lab safety rules are given by the instructor so that students can:','["avoid thinking", "work without injury", "finish early", "skip steps"]'::jsonb,1,'Safety is a priority.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.A',4,'Before powering a circuit, students should have the instructor:','["sign the lunch form", "leave", "check the wiring", "paint it"]'::jsonb,2,'A check prevents shorts.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.B',3,'Hazardous materials are grouped by:','["color only", "size of container", "price", "the type of danger they present"]'::jsonb,3,'Classes include flammable and corrosive.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.B',4,'A label with a flame symbol marks a material that is:','["flammable", "radioactive", "edible", "cold"]'::jsonb,0,'Symbols show hazards.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.C',3,'Used solder and chemicals are disposed of:','["anywhere", "according to posted procedures", "down the sink", "in any bin"]'::jsonb,1,'Follow waste rules.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.C',4,'Lead-free solder scraps and used batteries are placed in:','["the drain", "the regular trash", "designated recycling or waste containers", "a pocket"]'::jsonb,2,'Dispose properly.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.D',3,'Improperly maintained tools can cause:','["savings only", "better results", "safer shops", "injuries and poor-quality work"]'::jsonb,3,'Maintenance protects workers.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.D',4,'A dull saw blade is dangerous because it requires more force and may:','["slip or bind", "shine", "become sharper", "cut itself"]'::jsonb,0,'Dull tools slip.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.E',3,'A digital caliper is used to measure:','["weight", "small dimensions precisely", "temperature", "room size"]'::jsonb,1,'Calipers give precise length.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.E',4,'A multimeter set to measure voltage is connected to a circuit:','["backwards on purpose", "in series", "in parallel across the component", "only when unpowered"]'::jsonb,2,'Voltage is measured across.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.F',3,'A designer reviewing a circuit for quality and reliability looks for:','["decorations", "paint", "logos", "weak points that could fail"]'::jsonb,3,'Review for risks.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.F',4,'Using a resistor with an LED is a design choice that improves:','["reliability by limiting current", "price", "color", "brightness always"]'::jsonb,0,'Resistors protect LEDs.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.G',3,'Regulations from OSHA exist to protect workers'' health and:','["hobbies", "safety", "hours", "pay"]'::jsonb,1,'OSHA sets rules.','original'),
('127.403.d.9.G',4,'A company that follows industry standards and regulations is more likely to have products that are:','["untested", "unsafe", "safe and accepted by customers", "banned"]'::jsonb,2,'Compliance builds trust.','original'),
('127.401.d.1.G',4,'A wind-tunnel test of a small airplane shape before building the real plane is an example of using a:','["published law", "hypothesis only", "final product", "physical scale model"]'::jsonb,3,'Scale models test performance cheaply.','original'),
('127.401.d.1.H',4,'A statement like ''objects in free fall near Earth accelerate at about 9.8 m/s²'' is best classified as a:','["law describing a regular pattern", "personal opinion", "unrelated claim", "guess"]'::jsonb,0,'Laws summarize observed regularities.','original'),
('127.401.d.9.D',4,'Household outlets are wired in parallel so that each appliance receives the same:','["resistance", "voltage", "current", "power"]'::jsonb,1,'Parallel branches share voltage.','original'),
('127.401.d.9.E',4,'A 6 ohm resistor carries a current of 2 A. The voltage across it is:','["8 V", "3 V", "12 V", "4 V"]'::jsonb,2,'V = IR = 12.','original'),
('127.401.d.11.B',4,'A metal spoon left in a hot cup of soup feels hot at the handle because heat moves through the metal by:','["radiation only", "convection only", "fission", "conduction"]'::jsonb,3,'Heat travels through solids by conduction.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
